    "extraction_notes": [
      "The supplied datasheet contains usable plotted curves in Fig. 1 through Fig. 4 on p. 2. Curve points are manual digitizations of visible plotted lines and are not interpolated from tabulated values.",
      "Fig. 1 contains separate typical forward-characteristic curves at Ta = 25 degC and Ta = 100 degC; the plotted forward-current axis is logarithmic.",
      "Fig. 2 contains separate typical reverse-characteristic curves at Ta = 25 degC and Ta = 100 degC; the plotted reverse-current axis is logarithmic.",
      "Fig. 3 is the typical junction-capacitance curve at Ta = 25 degC and f = 1 MHz; the electrical characteristics table gives CT = 30 pF at VR = 5.0 V.",
      "Fig. 4 is included as a usable power-derating rating curve even though it is outside the minimum diode forward-IV, leakage, capacitance, and recovery fitting inputs.",
      "The electrical characteristics table publishes typical and maximum forward-voltage values at IF = 100 mA, 500 mA, and 1000 mA; all available rows are transcribed in forward_voltage_points.",
      "The reverse-current table publishes maximum values of 15 uA at VR = 5 V and 25 uA at VR = 8 V; reverse_current records the highest-voltage row.",
      "No reverse-recovery time or measured breakdown-voltage/breakdown-current characteristic is published. The 10 V VRRM, VRMS, and VDC entries are ratings rather than breakdown measurements."
    ],
